  Steinberg ASIO SDK 2.3.4          https://www.steinberg.net/developers/
    ⚠ CHANGED 2026-08-24 — THIS NOW SHIPS. This entry used to open "ONLY IN A BUILD MADE WITH
    ARTLUX_ENABLE_ASIO=ON; default builds compile JUCE_ASIO=0 and link nothing of Steinberg's."
    That is no longer true: ASIO is ON BY DEFAULT for every Windows build, including released
    installers, because on an interface with its vendor driver installed it is the only route to
    outputs 3 and up (measured, below). A build without it is now the deliberate exception,
    produced with ARTLUX_ASIO=0.
    WHAT IS COMPILED IN: interface headers only — and they come from JUCE, not from a download.
    JUCE 8.0.14 VENDORS asio.h / asiosys.h / iasiodrv.h at modules/juce_audio_devices/native/asio/,
