    LICENSE.md, and uses them unless JUCE_ASIO_USE_EXTERNAL_SDK=1. So no Steinberg file is fetched,
    committed or redistributed by this project at all. No Steinberg .cpp, no library, no DLL. The ASIO
    DRIVER itself is the audio interface vendor's, installed by the user with their hardware,
    loaded at runtime by COM — we neither ship nor link it.

    WHY IT IS NEEDED AT ALL — this is not a latency luxury. Measured on a Scarlett 6i6 2nd gen,
    same machine and cables, 2026-08-21: on the generic USB audio-class driver the device opened
    SIX channels on every WASAPI mode; with Focusrite's own driver installed it opened TWO, on
    every mode, at every requested count. Vendor drivers commonly expose only outputs 1-2 to
    Windows and route the rest through ASIO alone. For those interfaces ASIO is the only way to
    reach outputs 3 and up, so a Windows build without it cannot drive a multi-speaker rig on the
    hardware most venues own.

